//
//  Secrets.example.xcconfig
//  RecipeTest
//
//  Copy this file to `Secrets.xcconfig` — which is gitignored — and fill in real values.
//  `new-project.sh` does the copy for you on a fresh project.
//
//  Debug.xcconfig and Release.xcconfig `#include?` the copy, so a missing file is not a
//  build error; keys simply resolve to empty.
//
//  To read a value at runtime, surface it through Info.plist:
//
//      <key>SomeAPIKey</key>
//      <string>$(SOME_API_KEY)</string>
//
//  then read `Bundle.main.object(forInfoDictionaryKey: "SomeAPIKey")`.
//
//  Note: a value containing `//` must be escaped, since xcconfig treats it as a comment:
//
//      SOME_URL = https:$()//example.com
//

// SOME_API_KEY =
